WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:04.200
While Republican Senator Ted Cruz was flying
back and forth from Cancun, Mexico, late two

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.200
weeks ago, Democratic New York Congresswoman
Alexandria Ocasio Cortez was raising millions

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:16.420
of dollars for Ted Cruz's Texas constituents
and was volunteering at the Houston Food Bank

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.900
for Ted Cruz's constituents.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.019
Now, Ted Cruz, thank AOC.

00:00:22.019 --> 00:00:23.230
No, he didn't.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.439
Did Texas Gov..

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:29.720
Greg Abbott thank AOC and Better O'Rourke
and all the other Democrats who fundraised

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:30.720
for Texans?

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.720
They didn't, did they?

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.980
Thank AOC and other Democrats who flew to
Texas and went to work at the Houston Food

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.540
Bank to help Ted Cruz's constituents know
they didn't thank them for that either, either.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.870
And when Ted Cruz finally mentioned AOC, it
was Friday during his CPAC speech.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.080
We saw this clip earlier during our Ted Cruz
clip.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.540
Here it is again.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:01:04.100
Here is Ted Cruz making fun of AOC for her
experience during the January 6th Trump riots.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.100
Bernie.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.650
Is wearing mittens.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:19.659
And AOC is telling us she was murdered.

00:01:19.659 --> 00:01:26.550
And the media desperately, desperately, desperately
wants to see a Republican civil war.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:33.000
Now, what is Ted Cruz even talking about,
aside from just being a disgusting human being?

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.850
Ted Cruz is referring to the Twitter exchange
in which AOC had tweeted that, quote, There

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:43.140
must or not not quote, which she tweeted that
there must be an investigation of Robin Hood

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.990
for their role in the GameStop fiasco.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:47.730
And Ted Cruz retweeted AOC saying, I fully
agree.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:51.890
And AOC, instead of sort of accepting Ted
Cruz's, I guess, bipartisanship, AOC tweeted

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:57.050
a rebuke of Ted Cruz saying, quote, I'm happy
to work with Republicans on this issue where

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.270
there is common ground.

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:01.010
But you almost had me murdered three weeks
ago.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.130
So you can sit this one out.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:07.690
Happy to work with almost any other Republicans
that aren't trying to get me killed.

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.610
In the meantime, if you want to help, you
can resign.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:14.790
Now, some people loved this response from
AOK, saying it's AOC standing by her principles,

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:18.319
regardless of whether on this one issue, Ted
Cruz agrees with her.

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:24.950
Others were sort of upset that AOK responded
aggressively to a senator saying, I want to

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.420
do I agree with you on this particular issue.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:32.900
Now, Ted Cruz is so disgusting that I do tend
to side with ABC on this particular one.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:38.730
But this is less about AOC and more about
the fact that even Republicans from Texas,

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:42.950
who did nothing for their constituents during
the storm, can't simply thank AOC for what

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:44.010
she did do for Texas.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.170
AOC has done more for Texans than their own
senator.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:47.860
Dozens of people died in Texas.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:52.360
AOK helped them, raised money, went to Texas,
went to a Houston food bank and worked.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.390
Ted Cruz went to Cancun and he's making fun
of the the you know, everybody lighten up

00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:02.069
is the type of thing people say when they
failed to deal with something serious and

00:03:02.069 --> 00:03:05.140
they want everybody else to take it less seriously.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:09.970
That's how they tell everyone not to worry
about it.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:14.440
Now, maybe people like Ted Cruz, C.A.C., as
a sucker for helping Texans.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:18.430
What I mean is she didn't have to do it.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.080
Like, legally speaking, Texans aren't her
constituents.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.080
She's the sucker.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.440
Maybe that's the view Ted Cruz has.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:26.800
AOC was suckered into helping people who don't
even get to vote for her one way or the other.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:31.300
Either way, these are really pathetic people
and we can only hope that they are eventually

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.300
held accountable.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:36.330
And like I said last week, unfortunately,
with Ted Cruz's next election, if he chooses

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:41.780
to run for reelection still four years away,
I'm not super optimistic that this entire

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:45.080
fiasco is really going to hit him in any way
that it will actually hurt.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.349
I hope to be wrong.

00:03:46.349 --> 00:03:51.550
But I mean, you know, when a Democratic New
York congresswoman is doing more for Texas

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:55.640
constituents than their own senator who's
trying to escape to the beach in Mexico, you

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:57.780
know that one of two things is going on.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:58.780
No.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:03:59.780
One, either.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:02.769
Voters really don't care what their elected
officials do, and they care only about what

00:04:02.769 --> 00:04:04.430
they say, which is quite probable.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:10.180
Or two, there may not we may just not have
a system that has consequences for bad actors

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:15.239
in the political system, in which case we
have to figure out other ways to win these

00:04:15.239 --> 00:04:16.239
elections.

00:04:16.239 --> 00:04:21.519
Probably some combination of the two.

